Flock's icons for Linux, installed into /usr/share/icons/hicolor by the packages:

- scalable/apps/dev.flock.Flock.svg: the app icon (design/logo/flock-app-icon.svg).
- symbolic/apps/dev.flock.Flock{,-stopped,-warning}-symbolic.svg: the tray icon by state, the
  logomark of design/logo/flock-logomark-black.svg; stopped is dimmed, a warning adds the ember
  badge, as on Windows and macOS (design/icongen). GNOME recolors -symbolic icons for its top
  bar, KDE through the ColorScheme-Text class.
- symbolic/apps/dev.flock.Flock-sites-symbolic.svg: the globe for sites (Sites pane, Logs,
  setup). Themes draw web-browser-symbolic as different things or not at all (GTK then shows its
  red missing-image icon), so the app ships its own.

The launcher, ../dev.flock.Flock.desktop, goes to /usr/share/applications; its name matches the
app ID, which is how the dock finds the window's icon.
